{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/909650-kiths-and-hurtlocker","id":909650,"title":"Kiths and Hurtlocker","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-07T17:59:27-07:00","id":909650,"title":"Kiths and Hurtlocker","content":"I noticed that Kiths are an exception to the no mortal Supernatural Merits for major templates rule.<br /> <br /> Some kiths like Ifrit grant such merits, and they can be used as a prerequist for other Supernatural Merits, such as the ones in the Hurt Locker.<br /> <br /> So an Ifrit could take Pyshic Onslaught for example, which requires Telekenisis or Pyrokenisis, Ifrits have Pyrokensis thanks to their Kith, but they spend glamour instead of willpower.<br /> <br /> Phantgasm or whatever its called could be taken by those of the Greys Kith.<br /> <br /> So does Hurtlocker change the balance between Kiths?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T19:03:35-07:00","id":909708,"title":"","content":"You still have to spend exp to get those additional merits, which you don't get to spend improving other aspects, so I don't really consider it game breaking. And that's assuming the ST allows Hurt Locker merits at all. I think it's a cool idea, being able to pursue the magic power inherent to your nature instead of more typical paths. I'd say that there's some precedent for it conceptually in the form of the Potent Kith merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T19:28:27-07:00","id":909732,"title":"","content":"I was actually talking to someone a while ago about it, and the general consensus was that it would be too cool for them <i>not </i>to be able to learn and use some of those Merits. Honestly, with the way Contracts are structured now, improving your Kith Blessing with ancillary Merits is no more powerful than increasing your Mantle or buying new Contracts, and in the long wrong it will prevent your character from being a bit more diverse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T19:47:52-07:00","id":909758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/909650-kiths-and-hurtlocker?p=909732#post909732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was actually talking to someone a while ago about it, and the general consensus was that it would be too cool for them <i>not </i>to be able to learn and use some of those Merits. Honestly, with the way Contracts are structured now, improving your Kith Blessing with ancillary Merits is no more powerful than increasing your Mantle or buying new Contracts, and in the long wrong it will prevent your character from being a bit more diverse.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, being able to purchase those same Merits can allow for hyperfocusing your character. That way, such a character is at a very big advantage within his element, but is found lacking in other aspects. That's not necessarily a bad thing for some people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T05:12:34-07:00","id":909982,"title":"","content":"As a general guideline, I feel like taking one playtest doc and combining it with another playtest doc is not the best idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T20:29:44-07:00","id":910517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/909650-kiths-and-hurtlocker?p=909982#post909982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a general guideline, I feel like taking one playtest doc and combining it with another playtest doc is not the best idea.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree. That being said, as long as the chosen Merits make sense for the character's concept, I'd allow it. Too much focus on a single ability is another issue that's best handled with clear communication with the ST. Even the Wizened have interests and traits outside their defining talent.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}